From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: hwcursor: scale the cursor in BGRA32, so its alpha is byte 3 on any host

When the renderer scales the picture up (the screen is bigger than the
game's resolution), SetHardwareCursorFromSurface converts the 8-bit cursor
to SDL_PIXELFORMAT_ARGB8888 and scales it with BilinearScale32, which reads
and writes the alpha as byte 3 of each pixel. ARGB8888 is a packed format:
on little-endian its bytes in memory are B, G, R, A, but on big-endian they
are A, R, G, B, so byte 3 is blue. The scaler then takes the blue channel
for the alpha: pixels with no blue (Diablo's browns and dark greys) become
fully transparent and the rest blend wrongly, and the cursor looks
see-through on a big-endian host (the PS3's PPE).

SDL_PIXELFORMAT_BGRA32 is the byte-order format with the alpha in byte 3
everywhere: it is ARGB8888 on little-endian (nothing changes on x86) and
BGRA8888 on big-endian. SDL_CreateColorCursor converts the surface to what
the video driver wants (X11: ARGB8888 in host order).

Test: tests/hwcursor-alpha-test.cpp (the scaled path and the X cursor read
back with XFixes, on amd64 and ppc64).

Forwarded: no

--- a/Source/hwcursor.cpp
+++ b/Source/hwcursor.cpp
@@ -83,9 +83,11 @@
 		newCursor = SDLCursorUniquePtr { SDL_CreateColorCursor(surface, hotpoint.x, hotpoint.y) };
 	} else {
 		// SDL does not support BlitScaled from 8-bit to RGBA.
-		SDLSurfaceUniquePtr converted { SDL_ConvertSurfaceFormat(surface, SDL_PIXELFORMAT_ARGB8888, 0) };
+		// BilinearScale32 reads the alpha from byte 3 of each pixel: BGRA32 has it there on any host
+		// (it is ARGB8888 on little-endian, BGRA8888 on big-endian, where ARGB8888's byte 3 is blue).
+		SDLSurfaceUniquePtr converted { SDL_ConvertSurfaceFormat(surface, SDL_PIXELFORMAT_BGRA32, 0) };
 
-		SDLSurfaceUniquePtr scaledSurface = SDLWrap::CreateRGBSurfaceWithFormat(0, scaledSize.width, scaledSize.height, 32, SDL_PIXELFORMAT_ARGB8888);
+		SDLSurfaceUniquePtr scaledSurface = SDLWrap::CreateRGBSurfaceWithFormat(0, scaledSize.width, scaledSize.height, 32, SDL_PIXELFORMAT_BGRA32);
 		if (ShouldUseBilinearScaling()) {
 #if LOG_HWCURSOR
 			Log("hwcursor: SetHardwareCursorFromSurface {}x{} scaled to {}x{} using bilinear scaling",
--- a/Source/utils/sdl_bilinear_scale.hpp
+++ b/Source/utils/sdl_bilinear_scale.hpp
@@ -15,7 +15,8 @@
 
 /**
  * @brief Bilinear 32-bit scaling.
- * Requires `src` and `dst` to have the same pixel format (ARGB8888 or RGBA8888).
+ * Requires `src` and `dst` to have the same 32-bit pixel format with the alpha in byte 3 of each pixel
+ * in memory (BGRA32 or RGBA32, on any host's byte order).
  */
 void BilinearScale32(SDL_Surface *src, SDL_Surface *dst);
 
